Linux-facing files of the device-driver environment for the Linux 6.1 kernel

The drivers of this repository that are ported from Linux are based on the
Android 6.1 kernel of the Pixel 7, as the vendor's drivers exist for this
kernel only. They use the device-driver environment (DDE) of Genode's
'dde_linux' repository, which follows a much newer kernel. Until Genode
26.05, the Linux-facing files of the DDE supported older kernels via checks
of the kernel version. These checks were removed from Genode in July 2026
(commit "dde_linux: remove no longer needed version checks").

This directory contains those Linux-facing files that the 6.1 kernel needs
in another form than the current 'dde_linux' repository provides. It mirrors
the structure of 'repos/dde_linux/src'. The files are taken unmodified from
Genode 25.11, the version the drivers were developed with. Their copyright
and license are stated in their headers.

All other files of the DDE come from the 'dde_linux' repository: the
Genode-facing code (C++ sources, lx_kit, the lx_emul API headers) and the
Linux-facing files that fit both kernels. The import file
'lib/import/import-pixel_lx_emul.mk' gives the files of this directory
precedence.


Following a change of Genode
----------------------------

The file 'tree_files.sha256' lists the Linux-facing files that the drivers
take from the 'dde_linux' repository, with the hash of the content they were
built and tested with. The tool 'tool/check_dde_drift' compares the files a
build has used with this list:

! tool/check_dde_drift <build-dir>

A reported file was changed, or newly introduced, by an update of Genode.
If it still fits the 6.1 kernel, the list is renewed by the tool's '--update'
argument. If not, its previous version is added to this directory.
